The {{Term/Store|Igneo Talus Titan|Igneo Talus Titans|Series, BotW}},<ref>{{Cite|'''Igneo Talus Titan'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> also known as the '''Huge Monster''',<ref name="Krane">{{Cite|That's right. I'm followin' the Great {{Color BotW|Blue|Daruk}}'s footsteps too! In fact, I hear {{Color BotW|Blue|Lord Daruk}} defeated a {{Color BotW|Red|huge monster}} at {{Color BotW|Blue|Lake Darman}}. I wonder what the {{Color BotW|Red|monster}} looked like...|Krane|BotW}}</ref> is a [[Sub-Boss]] in {{BotW}}. It is exclusive to {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack.

==Characteristics==
{{Compendium/Extract|Igneo Talus Titan}}
The Igneo Talus Titan is a sub-species of [[Igneo Talus]] that has achieved an enormous size by remaining hidden in [[Lava]].<ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|This Monster is an Igneo Talus subspecies that is camouflaged as molten rock. It lives in lava for many years before emerging at an enormous size. It is wildly powerful and emits a tremendous amount of heat, causing a constant updraft in its vicinity. This monster is so fearsome it has earned the title of Titan.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> 100 years ago, [[Daruk]] battled the Titan as part of him [[Divine Beast Tamer's Trial]].<ref name="Krane"/><ref>{{Cite|♪Crawling flame on a mighty peak.<br/>{{Color BotW|Blue|Rudania}}'s Champion, never weak.♪<br/>♪The hero's power shall grow.<br/>Seek trials {{Color BotW|Blue|monuments}} show.♪<br/>♪One, {{Color BotW|Red|stop of titan of molten stone}}.<br/>Two, {{Color BotW|Red|follow rings of light alone}}.♪<br/>♪Three, {{Color BotW|Red|survive lava's fiery fate}}.<br/>Champion, trials await!♪|Kass|BotW}}</ref> During the "[[EX Champion Daruk's Song]]" [[Main Quest]], [[Link]] is tasked with following in Daruk's footsteps and facing the same Trial.<ref>{{Cite|I applaud your courage in coming here. The locations that will be revealed to you are of trials that will enhance the power sleeping within. Do not let your guard down...|Monk|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Divine Beast Tamer's Trial<br/>{{Big|'''Igneo Talus Titan'''}}|Game Screen|BotW}}</ref>

The Igneo Talus Titan appears at the northern shore of [[Lake Darman]], where it lies in the Lake's Lava and emerges as it is approached. Its characteristics and attack patterns are for the most part identical to the common Igneo Talus; its body is encased in molten rock and it attacks by launching its arms at Link, which are then shortly regrown. It can also attack by slamming its arms into the Lava, creating a fiery splash. Its heated body also creates [[Updraft]]s of hot [[Wind]] around it.<ref name="Compendium"/> Link can use these to [[Paraglider|Paraglide]] to its weakness, which is the Ore Deposit protruding from the top of its head. However, coming in direct contact with the Titan's molten body will catch Link on [[Fire]]. To avoid this, Link can attack the Titan with [[Ice]] [[Weapon]]s to cool it down and stun it temporarily, or he can approach it while wearing the [[Fireproof Armor]] if it has been enhanced twice by a [[Great Fairy]] for the [[Fireproof]] Set Bonus. Notably, the Igneo Talus Titan does not leave Lake Darman, requiring that Link glide over if he intends to strike its Ore Deposit directly.

After the Igneo Talus Titan is defeated, the [[Kamia Omuna Shrine]] rises from the ground nearby, thereby completing the Titan's Trial.

Like the [[Molduking]], the defeat of the Igneo Talus Titan does not count towards its respective [[Medal of Honor]].

